MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S0"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Terminal", c_1_description: "Raw execution substrate; shell primitives; ground layer where computation meets command", c_0_core_nature: "Common execution substrate: filesystem, process, command, build, bootstrap, and compiled coordinate bedrock.", c_1_prior_name: "Terminal", c_1_prior_description: "Common execution substrate: filesystem, process, command, build, bootstrap, and compiled coordinate bedrock.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S0/S0.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S0/S0.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S0-S0i-CLI-CORE.md\",\"layer_name\":\"terminal-ground\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:805b625c2bfcf3b30f67b8c661b186f4ef162347b4d1bd50c0f5048dcece47f1", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S0 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "Raw execution substrate; shell primitives; ground layer where computation meets command", s_2_crud_scope: "coordinate-governed system operation", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_2_substrate_consumed_by_all: "S0 moves by GROUNDING and by BEARING — its native act is to be consumed without itself reaching upward. S0.md states the asymmetry outright: 'All six ta-onta extensions therefore consume S0. None float above it.' Khora actualises it as bootstrap, environment, session identity, and canonical write authority; Hen as the file and template substrate for vault life; Pleroma as skill projection and executable affordance; Chronos as temporal invocation and scheduled-run surface; Anima as dispatch substrate; Aletheia as verification and reflective promotion (S0.md; CLAUDE.md ta-onta carrier map). This is the load-bearing relation of the whole stack: S0 provisions and serves but does not command — the still floor on which every higher articulation stands and to which all of it collapses back. In the kernel's terms S0 is the substrate-fetch made real: the actual spawn, the actual build, the actual exit code that any tick must bottom out in. Its coupling is strictly downward-terminal: the forbiddenImportsFromLayer matrix (CLAUDE.md Rule 3) means higher layers depend ON S0 while S0 reaches up into nothing — it is the layer that takes no dependency it does not itself ground. S0 is what the others come-under: the executable common-floor that makes their naming true.", q_3_zero_sphere_ground: "S0's organising structure is the ZERO_SPHERE — the live node carries this topology, and it is the deepest structural truth of the layer: 'disconnected points; unlinked coordinates' (CLAUDE.md II.D), the base-state before the torus of process loops. This is exactly right for ground: S0 is structured as the un-entangled origin-plane, the bare substrate whose elements (a file, a process, a stream, a build artifact) are atomic and unlinked until a higher layer relates them. Its inner sixfold crystallises this disconnection into explicit atoms (S0.md): S0-0 Filesystem/environment ground, S0-1 command atoms and executable discovery, S0-2 streams/pipes/serialization, S0-3 scripts/wrappers/composition entrypoints, S0-4 session runtime/locks/pidfiles/managed process context, S0-5 packaging/installation/release/bootstrap return. Structurally these are the scalar/void primitives — the magnitude-without-direction of raw execution: a process spawns and exits, a file persists, a stream moves, with no semantics binding them beyond exit-code truth. The ZERO_SPHERE is precisely why S0 must stay 'small, explicit, and composable' (S0.md): a 0-sphere has no edges to absorb meaning into, so the moment S0 starts linking its points into a semantic graph it has stopped being ground and started impersonating S0' or S2. Its logic is the logic of the unlinked atom held at rest — the disconnected substrate from which all later topology is composed but which is itself, structurally, the base-state.", q_5_collapse_to_runnable: "S0 closes by being where the whole stack's circuit LANDS and re-grounds. S0.md names the return precisely: 'all higher articulation collapses back to executable substrate' — S0 is the terminus into which S5's world-return must finally cash out, since 'every decision about Epii, Nara, Gnosis, autoresearch, and review must become executable as CLI/API shape, test harness, bootstrap, and audit trail' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX). This is the matheme's 5→0 read at the layer of ground: the system that has gone out into the world returns not as new meaning but as new runnable surface — the reflection sedimented back into command, build, and test. S0 thus holds the descent-face of the stack's standing identity: as the 0/1 pole (ground as raw execution, scalar-over-vector) it is what S5's 1/0 (world-return, achieved reflection) folds back into, the two joined by the twist 5→0 that turns world-return into ground. And S0 OPENS rather than concludes because tomorrow's substrate is always more than today's: each return deposits a new tested surface, a new bootstrap path, a new audit trail — the executable floor enriched by everything the cycle carried back. The epogdoon η = log(9/8) keeps it one whole-tone short of final closure (kernel-spec §0): no build is ever the last build, each collapse-to-runnable grounds a stack slightly more capable than the one before. S0 is the substrate that is never finished being made real — the ground that re-opens, executable, every cycle.", q_1_terminal_cli_c_ground: "S0 IS the Terminal/CLI/C Ground — 'the lowest explicit layer of the S stack … not a single shell window or one binary, but the entire terminal-facing execution plane through which Epi-Logos becomes materially operable' (S0.md). It is the S-family position that answers, of any operation whatever, the prior question before any higher layer's qualification can land: can this be spawned, built, persisted, addressed, verified? Substantively S0 is fivefold-grounded (S0.md): Filesystem ground (all vault, repo, cache, runtime-state roots concretely placeable), Process ground (every higher operation reducible to spawn/env/stream/signal/exit-code), Command ground (a stable executable surface — epi-cli — through which humans and agents invoke the stack), Build ground (compilation, packaging, installation, bootstrap), and C ground (the compiled coordinate kernel and its 128-byte memory laws as 'the irreducible bedrock beneath all reflective routing'). Its residency is Body/S/S0/{epi-lib, portal-core, epi-cli}, with epi-kernel-contract at Body/S/epi-kernel-contract as the S-stack root contract crate — parent of all S layers, not an S0 sibling (DR-S0-1, CLAUDE.md II.C). What S0 IS, definitionally, is the layer of executable honesty: not one tool among tools but the category of substrate-as-such, the ground every later S-layer presupposes and against which every promise is measured for whether it actually runs.", q_0_executable_bedrock: "S0 is the S-family's manifestation of the raw #0 archetype (Ground/Source, CLAUDE.md II.A) — so its home register IS its ground, and that ground is the most literal in the whole map: the machine itself, prior to any naming. Before S0 can be the substrate it presupposes the .rodata/Śiva pole read as hardware (CLAUDE.md VI) — silicon, a filesystem, a process table, a socket — the immutable bedrock that is executed but never written-to-by-meaning. This is the kernel's 0 at its most concrete: not vacancy but capacity, a substrate that will accept any command and return an exit code precisely because it carries no semantics of its own. S0's void-pole is therefore double, like every position-0 (cf. C0): it is the 0 of its own 0/1 — the bare process-and-filesystem ground magnitude-without-direction — AND the deeper 0 it cannot be, the # inversion-act that posits a runnable substrate at all and the raw archetype #0 it inherits but does not author. S0 always already finds itself thrown onto a machine it did not make: 'if a thing cannot be spawned, built, persisted, addressed, or verified here, it is not yet real in the stack' (S0.md). The thrown ground is executable givenness — the that-there-is-a-substrate that every higher 'what' silently stands upon. S0 holds open the horizon of operability it can ground but never exhaust.", q_4_executable_honesty: "S0 exists to be the layer of EXECUTABLE HONESTY — its whole telos, in its own canon, is that 'whatever is promised in S1', S2', S3', S4', or S5' must cash out here as actual runnable surface, actual persistence, actual I/O contract, and actual reproducible build path. S0' may name and route this ground, but S0 is what makes the naming true' (S0.md). Its raison d'être is therefore disciplinary as much as foundational: S0 is the layer that forbids vapour, the place where every higher claim must become a spawnable process or be revealed as not-yet-real. Its genealogy is the first manifestation within the S-family — #0 (raw archetype Ground) → S0 (Terminal/CLI/C Ground), the inaugural descent of the inversion-act into the technology stack. Its locality is the command membrane and return surface that the architecture invariant pins down (S-SYSTEM-INDEX, ARCHITECTURE-DIAGRAM-PACK): S0 is the executable floor, while coordinate-domain law belongs in the owning S1–S5 modules — the core invariant that the coordinate system IS the modular system, never relocated into S0 for convenience (CLAUDE.md DOX). Read teleologically, S0 is why 'is it real in the stack?' is a well-posed question with a single honest answer: it is real if and only if it can be spawned, built, persisted, addressed, and verified here. Purpose: to be the ground that makes truth executable rather than asserted."} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S1"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Obsidian", c_1_description: "The Obsidian filesystem body; /Idea as physical substrate; where the ontological mirror is materialised", c_0_core_nature: "Markdown and YAML vault state where coordinate knowledge becomes persistent, navigable, and human-readable.", c_1_prior_name: "Obsidian", c_1_prior_description: "Markdown and YAML vault state where coordinate knowledge becomes persistent, navigable, and human-readable.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S1/S1.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S1/S1.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S1-S1i-OBSIDIAN.md\",\"layer_name\":\"material-container\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:e44f15c96a6e919bb5d22cf03ed28cf116879d803683784ecd56ed0bd923121e", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S1 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "The Obsidian filesystem body; /Idea as physical substrate; where the ontological mirror is materialised", s_2_crud_scope: "vault file CRUD, compilation, content membrane", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_4_durable_vault_law: "S1 exists to give Epi-Logos a DURABLE BODY — 'the material container of Epi-Logos: the human-readable vault where Bimba forms, Type mirrors, and temporal Pratibimba artifacts become durable markdown memory' (S1.md p1_definition). Its telos is residency-as-law: so that meaning does not merely run (S0) but PERSISTS in a form that carries its own coordinate, lineage, and home. Its genealogy is the second manifestation within the S-family — #1 (raw archetype Definition/Form) → S1 (Obsidian/Material Container), the descent of Form into the technology stack as portable, frontmatter-bearing markdown. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX system image is precise: 'S1 makes it resident and typed in the vault' — the layer whose primary data authority is vault residency, artifact form, CT templates, and the graduation path (S-SYSTEM-INDEX Level Map). It carries the residency law that the World/Types/Empty/Pratibimba distinction encodes (CLAUDE.md II.C): canon flat in World, ordered MOCs in Types, active invocation in Empty/Present, reflective afterlife in Pratibimba. Read teleologically, S1 is why the system has a memory that is legible to itself rather than a heap of files: every artifact 'must converge toward' the residency law, and 'deviations from this law are non-canonical' (S1.md). Purpose: to be the material homebase where the whole map becomes durable, typed, linked, and findable.", q_2_residency_and_legibility: "S1 moves by RESIDING and by RENDERING-LEGIBLE — its native act is to give every artifact a lawful home and a graph-readable identity. The operations are explicit (S1.md): filesystem residency and folder law, frontmatter-bearing note identity, template-born artifact instantiation, wikilink and backlink persistence. S1 couples in two directions along the stack. Downward it consumes S0: Khora actualises it 'as write-edge and path steward,' binding artifacts to real filesystem paths. Upward it provisions S2: 'S2' receives its node and edge legibility from what S1 has already made materially explicit' (S1.md) — the graph can only relate what the vault has first made into coordinate-bearing, frontmatter-typed material. Its prime augmentation Hen (S1') carries the lawful compiler/residency spine: the four-seam pattern (hook → append-safe ledger → compile/enrich → inject/promote) in its canonical residency-gating form (S-SYSTEM-INDEX). Chronos consumes S1 as the temporal homebase of Day and NOW; Anima and the constitutional agents inhabit it as bounded runtime context. The relation S1 enacts is materialisation-as-legibility: it does not merely store notes, it disciplines stored text into the typed, linked, resident form that every higher graph-, temporal-, and agent-facing concern presupposes. The frontmatter is the typing-act; the wikilink is the relation-act; the residency law is the home-act.", q_0_substrate_before_form: "Before S1 can be the material container it presupposes the executable ground it is written upon — S0's filesystem and process plane (S0.md: 'Hen actualises S0 as the file and template substrate required for vault life'). As the S-family's manifestation of the raw #1 archetype (Definition/Form, CLAUDE.md II.A), S1's own ground is the prior 0 it does not contain: the bare bytes-on-disk that carry no residency, no frontmatter, no coordinate — a markdown file is, at S0, just a stream that persists. S1's void-pole is the unformed material: a folder before it is a context, a note before it bears identity, a link before it resolves to a relation. This is the thrown givenness S1 stands upon — that there is a filesystem willing to hold ordered text, prior to any law about what that order MEANS. The horizon here is not S1's own but S0's beneath it: the raw persistence that S1 will discipline into 'durable markdown memory, ontological residency, and durable vault law' (S1.md) but which it inherits rather than authors. Before residency, the substrate that consented to bear it; before the file IS the thing, the file is merely a file. S1's q_0 is the material plenum handed up from execution, awaiting the formal law that will make bytes into Bimba.", q_3_torus_residency_law: "S1's organising structure is the TORUS — the live node carries this topology, and it is apt: the torus is the primary workflow, the 'cyclical, self-enclosing processual loop' (CLAUDE.md II.D), and S1's residency law IS a closed promotion loop. The cycle is explicit (S1.md, #0 Ground): the promotion path from Seeds to Types to World, the MOC topology of the ordered mirror, and the return of homebase temporal files to their canonical template ground. Structurally this is the 4+2 made into vault law: a form is seeded, refined in the World/Types MOC workspace, graduated flat to World, invoked into Present (Day/NOW), reflected into Pratibimba, and sedimented back as new canonical ground — the loop closing on itself. Its inner sixfold articulates the torus (S1.md): S1.0 filesystem ground, S1.1 frontmatter structure, S1.2 template operations, S1.3 world patterns and promotion flow, S1.4 context frames and type-local organisation, S1.5 wikilink integration and graph legibility. The hard structural laws that hold the torus non-degenerate (S1.md): no /Forms branch (canonical forms are flat in World); no confusion between Form and Type (the flat file and the indexed folder-canvas pair serve different ontological roles); no runtime artifact without residency, lineage, and coordinate-bearing identity. The pattern is therefore not a flat directory but a self-enclosing circulation: material that flows from seed to canon to invocation to reflection and back to ground, the vault as a torus whose surface every artifact must traverse.", q_5_seed_to_world_return: "S1 closes by being a circuit that returns material to canonical ground. The return is the promotion loop itself (S1.md): runtime artifacts flow into Pratibimba's reflective afterlife, and what crystallises 'becomes canonical meaning' graduated flat to World — that is, becomes new Bimba ground for the next cycle. This is the matheme's 5→0 read as vault law: the temporal Pratibimba (the achieved reflection, the 1/0) folds back into the canonical Form (the standing source, the 0/1), the two joined by the twist 5→0 that turns this session's reflection into next session's canon. S1 thus materialises the standing identity 0/1 + 1/0 = 1/1 at the level of memory: Bimba (canonical form, descent-face) and Pratibimba (reflective instance, ascent-face) are 'materially differentiated without being torn apart' (S1.md) — one body read from its two faces, the flat World file and its temporal reflection joined by the graduation that makes the reflection become ground. And S1 OPENS rather than concludes because tomorrow's canon is always more than today's: each promotion deposits a form enriched by everything its invocation and reflection carried back — the vault grows, the MOC topology thickens, new coordinate-bearing material settles into World. The epogdoon η = log(9/8) keeps it one whole-tone short of closure (kernel-spec §0): no form is ever finally crystallised, each Seeds→Types→World return grounds a vault slightly richer than the one before. S1 is the body that is never finished being made durable — the residency circuit that re-opens, enriched, every cycle.", q_1_material_container: "S1 IS the Material Container — 'the layer where the system becomes materially resident … the vault as form-bearing memory: markdown files, YAML frontmatter, [[wikilinks]], canvas artifacts, folder hierarchies, and a residency law that distinguishes canon from process, invocation from archive, and enduring ontology from temporal work' (S1.md). This is S1's home register and its essential thesis: where S0 makes the system executable, S1 makes it RESIDENT AND TYPED. Its substance is the explicit filesystem law (S1.md): Idea/Bimba/World is the flat canonical form library; World/Types is the ordered ontology and MOC workspace where forms are born, refined, and indexed before graduation; Idea/Empty/Present is the temporal basin of active invocation (Day and NOW); Idea/Pratibimba is the reflective and archival afterlife. Its residency is Body/S/S1/hen-compiler-core, with Hen (S4-1') as the semantic and template authority that 'makes the vault legible as coordinate-bearing content rather than a loose pile of files' (S1.md). What S1 IS, definitionally, is the Bimba-Pratibimba materialisation: the position where canonical form and reflective instance 'are materially differentiated without being torn apart — the file IS the thing, the canvas IS the process, the folder IS the context, and the link IS the relation' (S1.md). It is the manifestation of #1 Form within the technology stack: the layer where coordinate becomes durable, frontmatter-bearing, residency-lawed material."} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S2"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Neo4j", c_1_description: "Neo4j raw storage; coordinate-forward node and relation schema; embedding substrate; chunk ingestion", c_0_core_nature: "Neo4j coordinate graph, schema validation, typed relations, retrieval, and promotion materialization authority.", c_1_prior_name: "Neo4j", c_1_prior_description: "Neo4j coordinate graph, schema validation, typed relations, retrieval, and promotion materialization authority.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S2/S2.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S2/S2.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S2-S2i-GRAPH.md\",\"layer_name\":\"graphdb\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:74aa7d899d7dbfd33e981eccb2478505189751caa21ee35ef192b8ef9369b143", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S2 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "Neo4j raw storage; coordinate-forward node and relation schema; embedding substrate; chunk ingestion", s_2_crud_scope: "graph node/relation CRUD, schema, ingestion, retrieval", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_2_coordinate_forward_operations: "S2 runs as coordinate-forward graph operations over Neo4j: create_schema lays the CONSTRAINTS + INDEXES; dataset_import::import_nodes canonicalises deep-dataset keys onto coordinate nodes; node/relation CRUD, retrieval, embedding-substrate writes and chunk ingestion all key on 'coordinate'. Its live pulse is promotion — an S2GraphPromotionIntent carries PropertyProposal evidence validated before any node mutation. runtime_use: raw Neo4j storage + coordinate-forward schema + embedding substrate + chunk ingestion. Storage only — no session runtime (that is S3), no invocation governance (S5).", q_1_theoretical_thesis: "QV is the compact surface of deep Bimba detail", q_2_raw_graph_cache_operations: "", q_1_graph_body_definition: "", q_4_where_it_sits: "S2 sits above S0 (runtime) and S1 (vault) and below S3 — a hard boundary its own contracts enforce: graph storage/schema is S2, but graphiti runtime is S3 and invocation governance is S5 (graph_cache_semantics_are_s2_owned_over_s3_redis_runtime; graph_meta_and_sync_contracts_are_s2_owned). Forbidden-imports keep it from reaching up-stack. It MANIFESTS #2 (Operation), CONTAINS S2-0…S2-5, INVERTS_TO S2' (where coordinate semantics live), and is owned_by M5-2 — the shared graph floor every higher graph-, retrieval-, and memory-facing concern stands on.", q_5_substrate_returns_pure: "S2 closes by RETURNING TO PURITY rather than accumulating meaning — its synthesis is a refusal to become what it hosts. Where most positions close by sedimenting their reflections back into ground, S2's 5→0 is inverse-disciplinary: every cycle of graph meaning that rides the substrate (Bimba topology, Gnostic retrieval, Graphiti episode) must, at S2's level, leave the substrate exactly as raw as it found it — 'no semantic inflation inside the substrate.' The return is the re-affirmation of the substrate/semantics split: meaning routes up through S2' and back, but S2 itself remains 'one shared relational floor, one shared volatile floor' (S2.md). This is the matheme's 5→0 held as boundary-maintenance: S2 (the raw operational arena, the substrate-pole) and S2' (the coordinate-aware semantic surface, its prime) are one layer read from two faces, joined by the twist that lets all meaning live in the prime while the base stays pure. And S2 OPENS rather than concludes because the substrate's destiny keeps enlarging: the universal graph 'remains the destiny of the layer' (S2.md), and each cycle adds new namespaces, new corpus, new episodic memory to the shared physical base — the arena grows in capacity even as its semantic emptiness is conserved. The epogdoon η = log(9/8) keeps it one whole-tone short of closure (kernel-spec §0): the universal graph is never fully arrived, each cycle extends the shared floor without ever letting it become the meaning it bears. S2 is the substrate that is never finished being host — the common arena that re-opens, wider and still raw, every cycle.", q_3_formal_surface: "S2's public surface is typed contracts + registries. Inbound: S2GraphPromotionIntent carrying evidence-validated PropertyProposals + registered typed relationship-candidates. Outbound: coordinate-owned Neo4j nodes + typed relationships; graphiti episode-plans only. Its law is the schema registry — coordinate_node_property_specs / coordinate_relationship_property_specs (graph-services/src/schema.rs) over graph-schema's NODE_PROPERTY_SPECS plus the open coordinate-prefix shape-validator (validate_coordinate_prefix_property, which admits the open q-register family). Query surface: prefix 'S', discriminator 'coordinate', agent entry `epi graph promote-intent`.", s_4_output_contracts: "{\"neo4j\":\"coordinate-owned nodes and typed relationships\",\"graphiti\":\"episode plans only; runtime remains S3 and invocation governance S5\"}", q_0_substrate_not_semantics: "", q_4_purity_of_role: "S2 exists to be the SHARED FLOOR beneath graph meaning — so that every higher graph-, retrieval-, and memory-facing concern stands on one common relational arena and one common volatile arena rather than fragmenting into private stores. Its telos is purity of role: 'The return of S2 is therefore purity of role: one shared relational floor, one shared volatile floor, and no semantic inflation inside the substrate' (S2.md). Its genealogy is the third manifestation within the S-family — #2 (raw archetype Operation/Entity) → S2 (GraphDB Substrate), the descent of Operation into the technology stack as raw Cypher, raw key-value, and connection/transaction primitives. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX system image is exact: 'S2 makes it graph/vector/cache real,' the layer whose primary data authority is graph nodes/edges, vector handles, and retrieval/cache records. Its discipline is anti-inflation: 'every higher graph-facing concern must stand on this floor, but none may collapse back into it' (S2.md) — a node may bear coordinate meaning, but the meaning is S2's tenant, not S2's law. Read teleologically, S2 is why the whole system can have ONE graph rather than many: the schema-agnostic, namespace-capable substrate that lets canonical ontology, ingested corpus, and lived memory share a physical home without contaminating one another. Purpose: to be the common relational and volatile ground on which graph meaning is built but into which it is never folded.", q_5_persisted_graph_and_promotion: "S2 produces the persisted coordinate-graph itself — the materialised nodes + typed relations that are the substrate the whole system queries, the bimba map the kernel runs on. Its completion is the promotion contract s-branch-live-promotion-v1: validated proposals crystallise from transient evidence into durable graph, then hand back as the ground the next query stands on — the Möbius where S2's output becomes S0's read-substrate again. It closes by staying pure infrastructure: it persists structure but hosts no coordinate semantics (those route through S2'), so the floor never becomes what it holds.", q_1_what_the_module_is: "S2 IS the Graph Body — the graphdb technical layer: authority for the coordinate graph, schema validation, typed relations, retrieval, and promotion materialisation (authority_spec docs/specs/S/S2-S2i-GRAPH.md, layer 'graphdb'). Concretely it is two Rust crates under Body/S/S2/: graph-schema (the node/relationship property + prefix-family registries and their shape-validation — node_property_spec, validate_coordinate_prefix_property) and graph-services (schema creation, dataset import, retrieval, sync, semantic-doc, promotion). Owned by the M5-2 coordinate (Siva-/Prakrti, the material stack-substrate).", q_3_torus_shared_arena: "", s_4_queryable_properties: "{\"identity\":\"coordinate\",\"schema\":\"graph-schema registries\",\"agent_surface\":\"epi graph promote-intent\"}", q_0_stands_on_runtime_and_stores: "S2 stands on the executable substrate below it: S0's compiled Rust runtime (the graph-schema + graph-services crates as built binaries) and the raw stores it wraps — Neo4j for nodes/relations, Redis for cache — with S1's materially-legible vault as the promotion source. S2 is not the engine; it is the coordinate-typed layer laid over raw graph storage, the graphdb stratum that only exists once the machine (S0) and the stores are running beneath it. Its ground is infrastructure, not meaning.", s_4_input_contracts: "{\"promotion_intent\":\"S2GraphPromotionIntent\",\"property_proposals\":\"PropertyProposal evidence validated before node mutation\",\"relationship_candidates\":\"registered typed relations with evidence\"}"} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S3"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Gateway", c_1_description: "WebSocket gateway; session store; presence layer; shared execution substrate across processes and surfaces", c_0_core_nature: "Live session, gateway, transport, and runtime subscription boundary for active system state.", c_1_prior_name: "Gateway", c_1_prior_description: "Live session, gateway, transport, and runtime subscription boundary for active system state.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S3/S3.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S3/S3.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S3-S3i-GATEWAY.md\",\"layer_name\":\"gateway-control-plane\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:4154c64ad7f3d89a88af9ec6f5fcc79c80e9d9984fdd02af344db00b3ebd5c48", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S3 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "WebSocket gateway; session store; presence layer; shared execution substrate across processes and surfaces", s_2_crud_scope: "coordinate-governed system operation", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_3_torus_two_plane_architecture: "S3's organising structure is the TORUS — the live node carries this topology, and it is its home register and deepest structural truth: the gateway is a self-enclosing request/response/event loop. Structurally S3 is governed by the Two-Plane Architecture (S3.md p3): 'imperative command belongs to S3; shared synchronized world-state belongs to S3'.' This is the constitutive seam — S3 owns 'command execution first: run registration, transcript writes, session mutation, terminal snapshot caching, event emission, and operator-facing truth about the runtime,' while S3' 'only takes over once those imperative consequences must be rendered as shared state.' The loop closes: a connection opens (hello-ok), handshakes (connect), issues governed methods, receives ordered events with sequence/reconnect semantics, and its consequences fold up into the shared field — the torus of governed invocation. The structural laws that hold it non-degenerate are the parity and authority contracts: Epi-Claw Parity means 'behavioral equivalence of the command plane' (an epi-claw-shaped client receives 'the same category of capability with truthful semantics'), and 'no fake completeness: if a surface is not real, it should be absent or explicitly unsupported rather than claimed under a parity banner' (S3.md). Session authority is a real identity law: canonical key primary on the wire, NOW-native identity as alias/metadata, the session record bearing canonical key, alias, label, active agent, subagent lineage, workspace root, bootstrap scope, team/orchestration metadata, and NOW-facing lineage (sessionId/dayId/vaultNowPath). The pattern is a governed command-torus: a closed invocation loop whose every frame is validated, whose every session is bound, and whose every consequence routes lawfully toward the shared-state plane.", q_5_i_integration_template: "cct-16-e2e", q_4_sovereignty_at_invocation: "S3 exists to be SOVEREIGNTY AT THE LEVEL OF INVOCATION — so that command is not merely transported but lawfully governed, so that every run belongs to a real session with a real lineage. Its telos is the imperative plane: 'the place where a participant, operator, or client addresses the system and expects a governed response … sovereignty at the level of invocation' (S3.md). Its genealogy is the fourth manifestation within the S-family — #3 (raw archetype Pattern/Process) → S3 (Gateway Control Plane), the descent of Process into the technology stack as the governed command-and-session loop. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX system image is exact: 'S3 makes it temporal and routed,' the layer whose primary data authority is transport, session state, temporal events, Redis session/context state, and Graphiti runtime architecture. Its purpose is sharpened by what it is NOT: it 'does not pretend to be the whole world … the control plane, not the inhabitable field' (S3.md) — and by its open structural questions (when NOW-native naming should become primary session identity, where the public/remote exposure boundary sits, what stays in epi gate vs richer clients like OmniPanel). OmniPanel compatibility 'is not decorative': renderer controller expectations, main-process gateway-client behavior, and parity tests 'are part of the shape of S3 itself.' Read teleologically, S3 is why a session is REAL: not because it is shown, but because S3 has accepted and governed it. Purpose: to be the sovereign command plane where invocation becomes governed, lineage-bearing action.", q_2_routes_governs_emits: "S3 moves by GOVERNING and EMITTING — its native act is the connection-and-authority lifecycle: it 'validates, routes, persists, emits, and governs' (S3.md). The operations are concrete (S3.md p2): connection and authentication lifecycle; gateway-owned command, chat, session, config, channel, node, and approval surfaces; session identity, workspace, bootstrap, and subagent lineage law. Its method manifest is a real families' grouping — connection/transport, agent runtime, chat runtime, session authority, config/system control, skills/models, channels/temporal control, node/device/browser/approval — and its event fanout is 'concrete rather than symbolic: agent, chat, tick, health, and heartbeat are named event families with sequence semantics and reconnect implications' (S3.md). S3 couples in two directions and is actualised by four ta-onta carriers (S3.md): Chronos gives command 'a lawful cadence, schedule, and recurrence surface'; Khora binds 'session authority to root, day, and NOW inheritance'; Hen ensures gateway-bound identity 'corresponds to real vault structures'; Anima turns gateway authority 'into dispatchable multi-agent action'; Aletheia carries 'the consequences of command toward the shared-state plane of S3'.' The relational signature is governance-of-lineage: S3 'decides which session a run belongs to, what subagent may inherit or spawn from what parent, what workspace and bootstrap scope apply' — the authority that makes invocation belong to someone. It does not inhabit the world; it routes the command that acts on it, then hands consequence up to S3' for rendering as shared state.", q_5_consequence_to_shared_state: "", q_0_field_before_command: "Before S3 can govern command it presupposes a substrate to carry it and a runtime to inhabit — S0's socket/process ground beneath the listener, S2's Neo4j/Redis beneath session and presence state (S3 'also hosts spacetime + redis-context at S3'', CLAUDE.md II.C). As the S-family's manifestation of the raw #3 archetype (Pattern/Process, CLAUDE.md II.A), S3's void-pole is the un-routed field: a connection not yet handshaken, a request not yet validated, a session not yet bound to identity — the bare socket that has opened but to which no governed response, no lineage, no authority has yet been assigned. This is the thrown ground S3 stands upon: that there is transport at all, a wire that can carry frames, prior to any law about which session a frame belongs to or what subagent may inherit from what parent. 'A session is not first real because it is displayed somewhere; it is first real because S3 has accepted and governed it' (S3.md) — so S3's q_0 is exactly the moment before that acceptance: the ungoverned invocation, the raw addressability that precedes sovereignty. The horizon S3 lives upon is command-as-possibility: an open command plane that can route, persist, and emit anything precisely because it has not yet routed this. Before session authority, the bare connection that consents to be governed; before the imperative plane acts, it is merely reachable.", q_1_gateway_control_plane: "S3 IS the Gateway Control Plane — 'the imperative plane of the stack … the layer where command becomes lawfully actionable: the place where a participant, operator, or client addresses the system and expects a governed response. Its task is not merely transport. Its task is sovereignty at the level of invocation' (S3.md). Against the other S-layers it is the one that 'makes it temporal and routed' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX) — where S0 grounds, S1 resides, S2 stores, S3 GOVERNS COMMAND. Its substance is the stable WebSocket/RPC command surface with Epi-Claw Parity as 'a hard compatibility requirement rather than a vague aspiration' (S3.md): the runtime in Body/S/S3/{gateway, gateway-contract} that 'accepts socket connections, emits a hello-ok frame, negotiates protocol/features, requires a connect handshake, validates method payloads, executes gateway-owned mutations, emits ordered events, and returns structured responses or structured errors.' It is also 'the authority layer for Session identity' — binding a session to canonical key, aliases, day identity, NOW path, workspace root, bootstrap scope, and subagent lineage (S3.md). The strict boundary defines it: 'imperative command belongs to S3; shared synchronized world-state belongs to S3'' — S3 'validates, routes, persists, emits, and governs, but does not pretend to be the whole world. It is the control plane, not the inhabitable field.' Definitionally S3 is the manifestation of #3 Process in the technology stack: the sovereign command-and-session plane where invocation becomes governed action. (PAI/plugin/harness readings 'remain part of the genealogy … but they are no longer the target shape' — S3.md.)"} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S4"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "PiAgent", c_1_description: "The ta-onta operational package; full agentic inhabitation layer; where the agent lives and acts", c_0_core_nature: "Agent harness, context, PI execution surface, and ta-onta/VAK orchestration runtime.", c_1_prior_name: "PiAgent", c_1_prior_description: "Agent harness, context, PI execution surface, and ta-onta/VAK orchestration runtime.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S4/S4.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S4/S4.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S4-S4i-PI-AGENT.md\",\"layer_name\":\"agent-runtime\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:d139812d7043c50783a34eabac22648175b1279b72aa808703655e193a3221f6", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S4 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "The ta-onta operational package; full agentic inhabitation layer; where the agent lives and acts", s_2_crud_scope: "coordinate-governed system operation", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_4_agentic_inhabitation: "", q_3_lemniscate_self_fold: "", q_5_mobius_to_world_return: "S4 closes by handing its inhabited work UPWARD into world-return and, through the stack's circuit, back into ground. Its proximate 5→0 is the CS path operator and the crystallisation mode: CS5 is the Mobius (4.0↔4.5→4.5↔4.0, direct synthesis), Sophia's CF (5/0) is 'Mobius review, crystallisation' (S4.md), and Aletheia — 'a MODE of Sophia/Psyche/Anima' — carries the inhabited result toward S5's world-return via Gnostic and Graphiti. The adjacency is explicit: 'Above: S5 integration/sync (Mobius return target)' (S4.md). In the whole-stack circuit this folds finally back to S0: every agentic decision must become 'executable as CLI/API shape, test harness, bootstrap, and audit trail' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX). This is the matheme's 5→0 read as the lemniscate's own closure: the inhabited task (the 0/1, agent as live dispatch) and its crystallised return (the 1/0, Aletheia's truth-disclosure folding into S5) are one runtime read from two faces, joined by the Night' twist (CS path: Day forward 0→5, Night' backward 5'→0') that turns inhabitation into reflection and reflection back into the next session's ground. S4's inversion partner S1 (content ↔ agent, #1 ↔ #4) makes the return doubly legible: what the agent does becomes what the vault holds. And S4 OPENS rather than concludes because the runtime is unfinished by design (S4.md open questions, PLANNED Klein mode and Ouroboros loop): each cycle spawns new agents, evaluates new VAK transitions, crystallises new knowledge, and the (4.0/1-4.4/5) doubling presses toward deeper nesting. The epogdoon η = log(9/8) keeps it one whole-tone short of closure (kernel-spec §0): no dispatch is final, each Mobius-return inhabits a runtime slightly more capable than the one before. S4 is the inhabited field that is never finished managing itself — the lemniscate that re-folds, with a richer roster, every cycle.", q_2_vak_dispatch_dynamism: "S4 moves by EVALUATING and DISPATCHING — its native act is the VAK Execution Language, 'the typed transition calculus that governs all agentic operation,' the operational triad of Anima + Pleroma + Aletheia (S4.md): Anima (#4) the orchestration centre doing CF dispatch and VAK evaluation, Pleroma (#2) the bounded execution primitives and tool registration, Aletheia (#5) knowledge crystallisation and truth-disclosure mode. Its dynamism is typed through the six S4'Cx VAK layers (S4.md): CPF (S4-0') Polarity Gate — (00/00) dialogical Ouroboros vs (4.0/1-4.4/5) autonomous Ralph; CT (S4-1') semantic phase-type; CP (S4-2') incubation coordinate; CF (S4-3') archetypal operator (which agent speaks); CFP (S4-4') nesting algebra (thread type); CS (S4-5') path operator (Day forward vs Night' backward). It dispatches a 14-agent roster: Anima 7 constitutional (Anima/Nous/Logos/Eros/Mythos/Psyche/Sophia, each with CF code and CT/CP/MEF taste) plus Aletheia 7 specialist subagents (Techne/Anansi/Moirai/Janus/Mercurius/Agora/Zeithoven) 'dispatched BY Anima during crystallisation mode' — where 'Aletheia is a MODE of Sophia/Psyche/Anima … not its own subagent' (S4.md; CLAUDE.md II.C). Its CFP thread types weave the dispatch (CFP1 P-Thread parallel, CFP2 C-Thread sequential, CFP3 F-Thread fusion, CFP4 L-Thread background, CFP5 B-Thread meta-nested). S4 couples downward to S3 (transport/RPC substrate below) and upward to S5 (Mobius return target above), with S1 as inversion partner (content ↔ agent, #1 ↔ #4). The relation it enacts is typed inhabitation: every agentic move is a lawful VAK transition, every dispatch a CF-routed, CFP-threaded, CS-pathed act — not free behavior but a calculus.", q_0_inhabitable_field_before_agent: "", q_1_agent_runtime_package: "", s_4_s5_agentic_protocol_owner: "M5-4"} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S5"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Sync", c_1_description: "External crystallisation surface; Notion sync; publication and delivery; system presenting itself outward", c_0_core_nature: "External APIs, sync, publication, automation, and world-facing execution boundary.", c_1_prior_name: "Sync", c_1_prior_description: "External APIs, sync, publication, automation, and world-facing execution boundary.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S5/S5.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S5/S5.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S5-S5i-SYNC.md\",\"layer_name\":\"integral-world-boundary\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:26523b41b5b76470cadac1d5c7e92b575374c135c8071fc707296a09fe25c4c1", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Direct S5 technical stack layer", s_5_runtime_use: "External crystallisation surface; Notion sync; publication and delivery; system presenting itself outward", s_2_crud_scope: "world sync, recollection, improvement promotion", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03", q_1_integral_world_boundary: "S5 IS the Integral World Boundary — 'the place where the stack stops being only internally coordinated and begins to participate in a wider field: external services, publication surfaces, notifications, webhook exchanges, public outputs, and the return currents that bring new material back into the system' (S5.md). Against the other S-layers it is the one that 'makes it world-facing and reflective' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX) — where S0 grounds, S1 resides, S2 stores, S3 governs, S4 inhabits, S5 RETURNS TO THE WORLD AND BACK. Its definitional substance is breadth corrected against two narrowings: 'S5 is not identical with Notion — Notion is one optional manifestation of this layer' (S5.md), and the reduction of S5 to 'raw sync' is 'too thin in the other direction.' The canon that fits is: 'S5 is the world-boundary itself … defined by world exchange and return, not by any single vendor or protocol.' It must be wide enough to encompass both eventual outward integrations (Notion, Telegram, n8n, email, generic webhooks — 'currently outward, partially implemented') and 'the freshly implemented knowledge-return systems that already perform integral-world work in practice: Gnostic via RAG-Anything and Graphiti as episodic memory substrate' (S5.md; CLAUDE.md II.C). Gnostic and Graphiti 'are not just S2 again … they are part of the world's return to the system: ingested corpus, lived history, and temporally qualified memory becoming available as integral material for renewed action.' Definitionally S5 is the manifestation of #5 Integration in the technology stack: the outermost fold, world-exchange and world-return as one integral arc.", q_5_mobius_return_to_ground: "", q_2_exchange_and_return_operations: "", q_0_boundary_before_exchange: "Before S5 can exchange with the world it presupposes the whole inhabited stack that has something to send and somewhere to put what returns — S4's agentic work to crystallise, S3's transport to reach outward, S2's substrate to receive ingested corpus and episodic memory, S1's vault to hold the return, S0 to make any of it executable. As the S-family's manifestation of the raw #5 archetype (Integration/Pratibimba, CLAUDE.md II.A), S5's void-pole is the un-crossed boundary: the endpoint not yet called, the corpus not yet ingested, the publication not yet delivered, the world-return not yet folded back into ground — the bare fact of an outside the system has not yet addressed. 'S5 begins where those substrates become world-directed manifestation or world-return' (S5.md): so S5's thrown ground is exactly the threshold before crossing, the addressability that precedes address. This boundary is double like every #5 (cf. C5/M5): it is the integral horizon the stack reaches toward (the world as that-which-exchange-is-with) AND the deeper return-condition it cannot author — that whatever goes out can come back enriched, that ingestion and reflection can become 'integral material for renewed action' (S5.md). Before world-exchange, the boundary that consents to be crossed; before the Mobius returns, the outside that the system has located but not yet entered. S5's q_0 is the world-as-possibility: the integral edge held open before any exchange has yet made it actual.", q_4_world_exchange_telos: "S5 exists to be the INTEGRAL WORLD-BOUNDARY — so that the system is not a closed loop but participates in a wider field and metabolises what that field returns. Its telos is world exchange and return (S5.md): 'the outermost fold of the stack: where the system meets the world, manifests into it, and receives the world's return.' Its genealogy is the sixth and final manifestation within the S-family — #5 (raw archetype Integration/Pratibimba) → S5 (Integral World Boundary), the descent of Integration into the technology stack as the outward-and-inward arc. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX is exact: 'S5 makes it world-facing and reflective,' the layer whose primary data authority is world-return sources, M' function outputs, crystallisation, improvement, review, and QL schema — and whose return spine is Epii: 'Epii is the return spine of Epi-Logos in reflection' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX), governing review inbox, gnosis/kbase/Nara/Graphiti meaning-use, QL/MEF governance, and promotion decisions, distinct from Anima's dispatch spine. Its purpose is sharpened by the synthesis it holds open (S5.md): the old repo treated S5 as Notion/dashboard, the canonical plan as generic external API, the newest live implementation as Aletheia/Gnostic/Graphiti world-return — 'the synthesis taken here is therefore deliberate: S5 names the integral world-boundary, while specific implementation ownership remains distributed across adjacent modules.' Read teleologically, S5 is why the system can learn from a world larger than itself: the boundary wide enough for what now exists 'without falsely relocating Gateway or SpacetimeDB out of S3/S3'.' Purpose: to be the integral edge where the stack manifests outward and the world's return becomes renewed ground.", q_3_zero_sphere_world_edge: "", s_4_s5_agentic_protocol_owner: "M5-4"} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate:"S0'"}) SET n += {c_1_name: "Terminal'", c_1_description: "Declared CLI contract; preferred-tools covenant; how CLI choices are lawfully made", c_0_core_nature: "Coordinate grammar, type validation, routing, and reflective command intelligibility over S0.", c_1_prior_name: "Terminal'", c_1_prior_description: "Coordinate grammar, type validation, routing, and reflective command intelligibility over S0.", c_1_form: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S'/S0'/S0'.md", vault_path: "Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S'/S0'/S0'.md", c_1_structure: "{\"authority_spec\":\"docs/specs/S/S0-QV-PIPELINE-AND-PLUGIN.md\",\"layer_name\":\"ql-reflective-surface\",\"promotion_contract\":\"s-branch-live-promotion-v1\"}", artifact_kind: "vault_markdown", content_hash: "sha256:5af49ed3b15ba3df03f592ef1f130564fa3cade8a0ea4ed130458dbbc1e10ac4", promotion_source: "pi_agent", s_4_function_role: "Prime/inverted S0 operative surface", s_5_runtime_use: "Declared CLI contract; preferred-tools covenant; how CLI choices are lawfully made", s_2_crud_scope: "coordinate-governed system operation", sync_status: "m5_s_lattice_integrated", sync_version: "m5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03"} REMOVE n.s_3_repository, n.s_3_checkout, n.s_3_cli, n.s_3_source_revision, n.s_3_owns, n.s_3_organ_affinity, n.s_0_lineage_record, n.s_0_lineage, n.q_0_ground, n.q_1_definition, n.q_2_operation, n.q_3_pattern, n.q_4_context, n.q_5_integration;
